{# Games page, v1.0, 21 November 2026.

   WHAT IT IS. Three daily puzzles, each at two levels, the same for
   everyone in the town: a crossword (easy clues or cryptic), a sudoku
   (easy or harder) and Wee Wurd (an English word or a Scottish one). A new
   set at 06:00 UK time. The reason it exists is the habit: a puzzle is the
   one thing on a town site that people come back for every single day.

   HOW IT IS MADE. Nothing on this page is fetched from anyone else and
   nothing is generated by a service. The page is this markup; everything
   that moves is in /assets/js/games.js, which explains itself at the top.
   The crosswords are built in advance by scripts/make-games.mjs from the
   hand-written clue bank in data/games/clue-bank.txt, and sit in
   /assets/games/ as one small file a month. WHEN THEY RUN OUT the page
   says so: run the script with a later date before the last month ends.

   WHAT IT KEEPS. Progress and the days played stay on the reader's own
   device. The privacy page says so; keep the two in step.

   NAMES. "Wee Wurd" is Ian's name for the word game. Its colours are the
   site's own. Neither the well-known name nor its look is ours to use.

   Answers are never proper names in Wee Wurd. The crossword allows a few
   local ones (Largs, Alexander), as crosswords do. #}
